    {
      "id": "session:2026-10-15-3c0f074e",
      "type": "Session",
      "label": "First benchmark, the plan with scrapy, and node cards",
      "description": "Goal: Run the v0.2 benchmark and decide what follows.\nInstructions: No Anthropic key: run the benchmark with Claude Code subagents.\nDiscoveries: On small repos the graph ties with reading the code; the graph agent could not read files, so it never followed the source and lines every node carries. Node cards match the code's score with 63% less context.\nAccomplished: kg query tested and kg impact --type (#50); benchmark harness and v0.2 report (#51); plan issue #52 with scrapy as the large repo; five example graphs rebuilt (#54); #55 opened; context metric and hybrid strategy (#56); node cards with --brief and signatures (#57, open).\nNext steps: Proposed by impact: (1) let hybrid read the files a stale graph reports, (2) the rest of step 2 (document sections, quoted claims), (3) step 3, scrapy with 15 to 20 questions, (4) #55. Tags waiting for confirmation.\nRelevant files: bench/, docs/benchmark.md, src/kg/query.py, examples/agent/",
      "attrs": {
